  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-g-a">And sawlsceat is rihtast, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man symle gelæste á æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-a">And saulsceat is rihtast, þæt man symle geleste á æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-q">Pecunia sepulturę iustum est, ut aperta terra reddatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="13" corresp="#wit-g-a">And sawlsceat is rihtast þæt man symle gelæste á æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">And it is best that payment for the souls of the dead should always be rendered before the grave is closed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Seelengeld ist am richtigsten, dass man immer sofort entrichte beim offenen Grabe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And as for soul-scot, it is most right that it always be paid at once at the open grave.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 20.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
